    {
      "id": "001c7a8d-dec5-5079-9e1e-fad72d16c6f8",
      "name": "Understand the request",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput",
      "position": [
        620,
        20
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "=Message: {{ $json.text || '(no text)' }}\nVideo file attached: {{ $json.file_id ? 'yes' : 'no' }}\nLink: {{ $json.link || 'none' }}",
        "batching": {},
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "=You turn a Telegram message into a Renderster video job. The user writes a command or plain words, in any language.\nCommands:\n/auto [style]: edit the whole video. Styles: best-youtube (polished YouTube look), hyper (most energy, fast cuts, effects), clean (calm and minimal), hardcopy (dark cinematic narration: black text cards with a red keyword, stock footage, noir grade, tense score).\n/clips [number]: cut the best moments into vertical clips with captions, 1 to 10.\n/dub [language]: translate the speech and voice it in another language. Codes: en, pt, es, fr, de, it, nl, tr, ja, ko, zh, hi, ru, ar, id, pl.\n/transcript: subtitles (SRT) and the text.\n/help: explain the commands.\nPlain words map to the same jobs: \"make it dark\", \"cinematic\", \"documentary\" -> auto_edit hardcopy; \"energetic\", \"TikTok style\" -> hyper; \"cut it into shorts\" -> clips; \"in Spanish\" -> dub es.\nA video with no instruction gets auto_edit with the default style.\nIf there is no video file and no link, or the user only asks a question, use action help and answer in reply.\nDefaults: style {{ $('Settings').first().json.default_edit_style }}, clips {{ $('Settings').first().json.default_clip_count }}, dub language {{ $('Settings').first().json.default_dub_language }}, orientation vertical (horizontal only when asked, e.g. \"for YouTube\").\nreply: one short sentence saying what you will do (or the answer, for help), written in the language of the user's own words. A command or a link is not a language: if the message has no other words, reply in English. The dub language is not the user's language: \"dub this to Spanish\" gets an English reply."
            }
          ]
        },
        "promptType": "define",
        "hasOutputParser": true
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.9
    },
